Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:01:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/23] runtime: VideoToolbox low-latency rate control, config
 encoder_low_latency (default on)

The in-process hardware session asks VideoToolbox for low-latency rate control
(kVTVideoEncoderSpecification_EnableLowLatencyRateControl). Measured on an M5 Pro at
2272x1264 H.265 72 Hz: encode callback 12.6 ms -> 8.0 ms, and that 8 ms does not move
with bitrate (25/50), resolution scale (0.5/0.75), codec (H.264/H.265), preset
(speed/balanced), refresh (72/90), a real frame duration, CompleteFrames after each
frame, or pre-converted 4:2:0 input - it is the encoder pipeline floor. Low-latency
mode has no periodic IDR; keyframes come from ForceKeyFrame (client requests). The
relaxed retry drops the flag with the hardware requirement. Config test covers the
default and both values; the init log line says low_latency=on/off.
